&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpaca is seeking a Senior Cashiering Operations Associate to own client money movement across ACH, domestic and international wires, RTP, checks, and internal journals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is accountable for timely, accurate, and compliant cash processing, with a strong mandate to strengthen operational controls, reduce risk, and drive process quality. You will operate with a high degree of independence, exercise judgment on complex and high-risk transactions, and serve as a key partner to custodians and banking partners. The ideal candidate brings deep money-movement expertise, a control-first mindset, and clear ownership of outcomes in a fast-paced fintech environment.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ops Control Framework &amp;amp; Oversight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously strengthen controls across money movement workflows, ensuring adherence to firm policies, regulatory expectations, and data privacy standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, validate, and approve client money movement requests (ACH, wires, RTP, checks, journals) in accordance with firm policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process and release transactions accurately and within established SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile daily cash movements, deposits, and settlement activity to ensure accurate posting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and resolve exceptions, returns, rejects, and transaction discrepancies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary operational point of contact for custodians and banking partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review daily and monthly operational reports, including transaction coding oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate documentation and case tracking in Salesforce and internal systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure adherence to regulatory requirements, internal controls, and data privacy standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify operational risks and escalate suspicious or high-risk transactions appropriately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audits, reporting requirements, and special projects as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Operations, Compliance, Risk, and Technology to design and implement process improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and coach internal teams; contribute to playbooks, SOPs, and onboarding for cashiering workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Business, Economics, or related field — or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in financial services, brokerage operations, banking, or cashiering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience processing money movements (ACH, wires, checks, journals, RTP preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience interacting with custodians, clearing firms, or correspondent banks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of operational risk and fraud controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of attention to detail and accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, confident written and verbal communication with internal stakeholders and external partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently, prioritize competing demands, and elevate issues with context and recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Series 7 or additional FINRA licenses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Portfolio accounting or broker-dealer systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech or high-growth environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior ownership of SOPs, control frameworks, or audit support for cash/money movement operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or training operations team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail Orientation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Action &amp;amp; Ownership Mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Risk Awareness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear Communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsiveness &amp;amp; Follow-Through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidentiality &amp;amp; Professional Judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alignment with Alpaca’s company tenets
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay Curious&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have Empathy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Accountable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
